---
/**
 * Cancellations and refunds. This page exists because a service agreement may
 * imply payment. It states only what is true today: fees are agreed in a service
 * agreement, no money moves through this website, and the commercial terms are
 * still the owner's to set. No refund window, cooling-off period or penalty is
 * invented here.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import DocLayout from '../components/DocLayout.astro'
import { BRAND } from '../config/site'
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/ld'
---

<Base path="/refund-cancellation" extraLd={[breadcrumbLd([{ name: 'Cancellations and refunds', path: '/refund-cancellation' }])]}>
  <DocLayout path="/refund-cancellation" title="Cancellations and refunds" lead="No payment is taken on this website yet. Plan prices are on the pricing page; notice and refunds will be set before billing starts." meta={`Effective date to be confirmed · ${BRAND.legalName}`}>
    <div class="notice" slot="notice">
      <p>
        <strong>Draft — needs owner and legal review, and the commercial terms, before it is
        relied on.</strong> The commercial terms below are placeholders. {BRAND.legalName} has not
        yet set a fee, a billing period, a notice period or a refund policy, so none is stated
        here. This page must be completed from the service agreement template, not from this
        draft.
      </p>
    </div>


    <h2>1. No payment is taken on this website</h2>
    <p>
      This website is a set of public pages. It has no checkout, no payment form and no card
      handling, and it does not take money yet. Plan prices are listed on the pricing page; the
      7-day free trial on Basic and Pro is free and needs no payment.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Where your fees are set</h2>
    <p>
      If fees apply to your business's use of {BRAND.name}, they are agreed directly with{' '}
      {BRAND.legalName} in your service agreement, arranged through your business administrator.
      The listed plan prices are on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>; how they are billed,
      renewed and refunded will be added here before billing starts.
    </p>
    <p>
      The service agreement is the document that governs billing, renewal, notice and refunds for
      your business. Where this page and your service agreement differ, your service agreement is
      the one that applies.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Ending an access arrangement</h2>
    <p>
      Access to a workspace is arranged by arrangement, not by self-service subscription. To end
      it, speak to your workspace administrator, who will follow the notice process in your
      service agreement.
    </p>
    <p>
      The notice period, and whether any fee is payable for a part-period, are terms of your
      service agreement. They are not set on this page and are not yet set by {BRAND.legalName}.
    </p>

    <h2>4. What happens to your records</h2>
    <p>
      When a business's use of the service ends, its business data is returned or deleted at the
      administrator's instruction. Deletion is complete, with no history and no footprints.
    </p>
    <p>
      Export your records while you still have access. Products, ledgers, sales and registers can
      be exported to CSV or Excel at any time, and that export is yours to keep.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      Refunds, if any, are dealt with under your service agreement. {BRAND.legalName} has not
      published a refund policy, and this page does not state one. No cooling-off period, refund
      window or cancellation charge is claimed here, because none has been set.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of India. The forum for disputes, and any arbitration
      mechanism, are to be confirmed by {BRAND.legalName}.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Schedule to be completed by {BRAND.legalName}</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Fee, billing period, payment terms and applicable taxes.</li>
      <li>Advance paid, and its treatment on cancellation.</li>
      <li>Notice period required to end an access arrangement.</li>
      <li>Refund eligibility, and how a refund is claimed and paid.</li>
      <li>Dispute forum and any arbitration mechanism.</li>
      <li>Effective date.</li>
    </ul>

  </DocLayout>
</Base>
